# Telemetry Contract

When writing or changing OpenTelemetry metrics, traces, logs, resource attributes, or OTLP export config, follow the CreaRec contract:

https://github.com/CreaRec/CreaGrafana/blob/main/docs/telemetry-contract.md

Before shipping telemetry changes, fetch or re-read that doc (raw: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/CreaRec/CreaGrafana/main/docs/telemetry-contract.md) and verify the change matches it.

## Must follow

- Export **only** to Alloy via OTLP (`OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT`). Never point exporters at Loki, Tempo, or Mimir URLs.
- Set resource attributes: `service.name` (kebab-case, no version), `service.namespace`, `service.version` (optional but recommended), `deployment.environment` (`production` | `staging` | `local`). Prefer `deployment.environment` over `deployment.environment.name`.
- Emit all required bot metrics (prefix `bot_`); do not invent parallel names for the same idea:
  - `bot_updates_total` (counter, label `result`)
  - `bot_handler_duration_seconds` (histogram, optional `handler`, `result`)
  - `bot_errors_total` (counter, optional `error_type`, `handler`)
  - `bot_up` (gauge, no labels; `1` while healthy)
- Metric labels: only low-cardinality enums from the contract — `result` (`success` | `error` | `skipped`), `handler`, `error_type`. Never put `user_id`, `chat_id`, `message_id`, URLs, paths, free-text errors, or trace/request ids on metric labels.
- Root span per Telegram update: `bot.handle_update`. Span attributes may be richer than metric labels (`result`, `error.type`, sizes) but avoid raw PII. On failure: `recordException` + error status. Propagate `trace_id` into logs.
- Emit OTEL logs (not console-only) with `severityText` (`DEBUG`/`INFO`/`WARN`/`ERROR`; prefer uppercase). Prefer structured attributes (`handler`, `result`, `error_type`). Do not promote high-cardinality fields to Loki stream labels; keep streams on `service_name` / `service_namespace`.
- Export failures must not block business logic (warn and continue).

## Out of scope

Pure business logic with no metrics/traces/logs/OTEL config changes does not need a contract check.
